<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Hyprop yr distribution per unit rises 7 pct.</title>
<headline>Hyprop yr distribution per unit rises 7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Interest per debenture (cts)  76.347    vs   71.357</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			    0.153    vs    0.143</p>
<p>    Retained income		    0.03     vs    0.03</p>
<p>    Pre-tax				0.74     vs    0.08</p>
<p>    Tax				    nil	vs    0.02</p>
<p>    Interest received		  5.25     vs    5.44</p>
<p>    Turnover			    42.25     vs   37.15</p>
<p>    Abnormal item			0.67     vs    nil</p>
<p>Div payable: April 30</p>
<p>on register: April 11</p>
<p>Full name: Hyprop Investments Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that the decrease in vacancy of the lettable area in the portfolio together with firmer rental levels, should results in growth in distribution in the year ahead.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
